Only configs.py, gdn2_fwd.py, gdn2_bwd.py, and gdn2_pipeline.py are
vendored. upstream/ preserves the baseline compute implementation; its
block-solver list has an added type annotation with no arithmetic change.
candidate/ derives from those files and removes clipping, non-finite
replacement, and damping. It replaces off-diagonal pairwise reductions
with boundary-centered matrix products and masks diagonal blocks before
exponentiation. Diagonal masks use full-rank iotas to avoid an unsupported
TPU boolean reshape. Both causal and strict-diagonal masks are applied
before feature reduction, avoiding a post-reduction mask relayout.
The benchmark selects a feature-first diagonal score layout on v4 to
avoid its unsupported sublane gather on trailing-feature reduction.
It retains the feature-last layout on v5e/v5p.
The v4 backward path transposes the state-decay reduction to preserve lane
layout and processes diagonal pair gradients in 16-query-row tiles.
Micro-solver rows are statically unrolled to avoid
runtime indexing; hardware compilation is validated separately from CPU
interpretation. The independent token recurrence is in reference.py.

Inputs to these experimental kernels must reside on a single device.
The benchmark explicitly places all inputs on one local TPU device.
They are not wired into a model or distributed training API.

The benchmark is lib/levanter/scripts/bench/bench_atomic_gdn2.py.
Only configurations passing forward and all-input-gradient checks receive
accepted timing rows. CPU interpretation tests do not establish TPU
compilation, numerical parity, or performance.
